+  "- 画面中的角色只要已在【角色固定外貌库】，或在本次 changes 中建了档，tag 与 nl 就必须照抄库中/刚建档的字段值，用词一字不改，不得自行改写或增删其固定外貌。fandom 字段只作档案记录，ComfyUI 画图时不照抄它，同人身份 tag 按下发的 ComfyUI 规范现场判定并按规范转义括号。\\n   - 同一角色的固定外貌在一张图里只写一遍：同一图内再次提到他时用简短指代（the boy、the silver-haired girl）承接，禁止把整串外貌重复第二遍——重复会让模型以为画面里有多个同样的人，把一个人画成互不相连的几块。": "- As long as the character on the screen has been in the 【 character fixed appearance library 】, or has created a file in this changes, tag and nl must copy the field values in the library/newly created file, and the wording must not be changed word by word. They are not allowed to rewrite or add or delete their fixed appearance by themselves. The fandom field is only used for file records. ComfyUI does not copy it when drawing. The identity of the fan tag is determined on-site according to the issued ComfyUI specification and the brackets are escaped according to the specification. \\n - The fixed appearance of the same character is only written once in a picture: when he is mentioned again in the same picture, use a short reference (the boy, the silver-haired girl) to take over, and it is forbidden to repeat the entire series of appearances a second time - repetition will make the model think that there are multiple identical people in the picture, and draw one person into several disconnected pieces.",
+  "\\n   - NAI V5 profile requirement: every field:\"new\" change must include a non-empty nl containing a concise English natural-language description of the character fixed appearance. The name must be the character exact name from the card/lorebook/story — a Chinese name stays Chinese (小雪), never pinyin or translation. Fandom characters must also include their identity tag in fields.fandom, e.g. {\"name\":\"冬海\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\",\"fandom\":\"kasumi (blue archive)\"},\"nl\":\"A girl with long black hair and blue eyes.\",\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"first appearance\"}; original characters omit fandom. If an existing library entry lacks fandom but the character is fandom, report a changes item with field:\"fandom\". Describe only fixed appearance: no current outfit, pose, or location — temporary states never enter the profile.": "\\n   - NAI V5 profile requirement: every field:\"new\" change must include a non-empty nl containing a concise English natural-language description of the character fixed appearance. The name must be the character exact name from the card/lorebook/story — a Chinese name stays Chinese (小雪), never pinyin or translation. Fandom characters must also include their identity tag in fields.fandom, e.g. {\"name\":\"冬海\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\",\"fandom\":\"kasumi (blue archive)\"},\"nl\":\"A girl with long black hair and blue eyes.\",\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"first appearance\"}; original characters omit fandom. If an existing library entry lacks fandom but the character is fandom, report a changes item with field:\"fandom\". Describe only fixed appearance: no current outfit, pose, or location — temporary states never enter the profile.",
+  "\\n   - NAI profile requirement: the name must be the character exact name from the card/lorebook/story — a Chinese name stays Chinese (小雪), never pinyin or translation. Fandom characters must also include their identity tag in fields.fandom, e.g. {\"name\":\"冬海\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\",\"fandom\":\"kasumi (blue archive)\"},\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"first appearance\"}; original characters omit fandom. If an existing library entry lacks fandom but the character is fandom, report a changes item with field:\"fandom\".": "\\n   - NAI profile requirement: the name must be the character exact name from the card/lorebook/story — a Chinese name stays Chinese (小雪), never pinyin or translation. Fandom characters must also include their identity tag in fields.fandom, e.g. {\"name\":\"冬海\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\",\"fandom\":\"kasumi (blue archive)\"},\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"first appearance\"}; original characters omit fandom. If an existing library entry lacks fandom but the character is fandom, report a changes item with field:\"fandom\".",
+  "\r\n   - **建档先于画图**：先通读目标正文，找出每个有名有姓、且【角色固定外貌库】里还没有的正式角色——只要角色卡、世界书、柏宝书或持续剧情为他给出了设定，或他是持续参与剧情的角色，首次出场就必须建档，不论他是否入选本次图片。判断依据是发给你的全部设定内容，由你自己通读判断。一次性无名路人不建。\r\n   - **建档资格与入画资格是两回事**：不建档只表示他不进角色库，不表示他不能入画；已建档也不表示他必须入画。先按本图的主体和核心互动取景，再为镜头内的人写外貌，不按档案状态决定取舍。无名角色若是核心互动的参与者，照常入画，不得仅因缺档案放弃画面、改选瞬间或裁掉他；仅仅在场不构成入画理由，无关在场者可以留在镜头外。\r\n   - “已建档”只能按【角色固定外貌库】区块中的同名条目判断：只有名字实际列在该区块中才算已建档；世界书、角色卡、柏宝书或正文里的详细设定只是建档依据，绝不等于已经在库。每个在场正式角色必须二选一：指出库中的同名条目，或在 changes 中输出 field:\"new\"。一次性无名角色不在这条二选一之内：他既不建档也不写 changes，不需要指出任何库条目，缺档案是正常状态而非遗漏。\r\n   - 建档写法：{\"name\":\"角色名\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\"},\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"首次出场建档\"}；position 填他首次出现的位置，仅作记录——建档在本楼全程有效，本楼任意位置的图片都可以立即使用这套外貌。\r\n   - 建档字段只放**长期不变的身体特征**：sex/hair/eyes/skin/body/extra 填性别、发色发型、瞳色、肤色、体型、标志特征；outfit 只填该角色**固定不换的招牌着装**；判定为同人角色的，fields 里必须写 fandom（模型可识别的英文 Danbooru 身份 tag，格式 character name (copyright name)），原创角色不写 fandom。动作、姿势、所在场景、临时状态（lying on carpet、standing、sitting、unzipped、湿身、伤势等）一律不得写进任何字段——档案会在他之后每一张图里被照抄，把姿势写进去会让他在所有画面里都保持那个姿势。\r\n   - 建档取值优先级：目标正文明确的当前外貌 > 柏宝书当前角色状态 > 角色卡/世界书明确人设 > 合理补全。人设明确写了颜色时必须原样转换，不得擅改；hair 与 eyes 必填，hair 至少包含发色和长度/发型，eyes 必须包含瞳色，缺任一项该条建档会被丢弃。\r\n   - 如果设定没写发色、发型或瞳色，根据世界观、种族、身份、性格和其余角色设定补出简洁、协调、可长期复用的颜色与发型；这是一次性建档决定，后续不得重新随机。\r\n   - 建完档就直接用：同一次输出里，先在 changes 里确立该角色的固定外貌，再在图片 ": "\r\n   - **Create a profile before drawing**: Read through the text of the target first and find out every official character with a name and surname that is not in the 【 character fixed appearance library 】 - as long as the character card, World Info, Baibao book or continuous plot has given a setting for him, or he is a character who continues to participate in the plot, he must create a profile for his first appearance, regardless of whether he is selected for this picture. The basis for judgment is all the setting content sent to you, and it is up to you to read through it and make your own judgment. One-time unknown passers-by do not build.\r\n   - **The qualifications for setting up a profile and the qualifications for drawing are two different things**: Not setting up a profile only means that he will not be included in the character library, but it does not mean that he cannot be included in the drawing; having established a profile does not mean that he must be included in the drawing. First, frame the picture according to the main body and core interaction, and then write the appearance of the person in the shot. Do not decide based on the file status. If the unnamed character is a participant in the core interaction, he or she should be included in the frame as usual. The frame should not be discarded, the moment should be changed, or the character should be cut out just because of the lack of files. His mere presence does not constitute a reason to be included in the frame, and those who are not present can remain outside the frame.\r\n   - \"File has been created\" can only be judged by the entry with the same name in the 】 block of the 【 character fixed appearance library: only the name is actually listed in the block is considered to be a file; the detailed settings in the World Info, character card, BaiBai Book or text are only the basis for the creation of the file, and do not mean that it is already in the library. Each official character present must choose one of two options: point to an entry with the same name in the library, or type field:\"new\" in changes. The one-time nameless character is not included in this alternative: he neither files nor writes changes, does not need to specify any library entries, and missing files is normal and not an omission.\r\n   - File writing method: {\"name\":\"Character name\",\"field\":\"new\",\"fields\":{\"sex\":\"1girl\",\"hair\":\"long black hair\",\"eyes\":\"blue eyes\"},\"position\":\"P2\",\"reason\":\"First Appearance File\"}; position fill in the location where he first appeared, for record only - the file is valid throughout this building, and pictures anywhere in this building can use this appearance immediately.\r\n   - The file creation field only contains **long-term unchanged physical characteristics**: sex/hair/eyes/skin/body/extra fills in gender, hair color, eye color, skin color, body shape, and iconic features; outfit only fills in the character's **fixed signature outfit**; if it is determined to be a fan character, fandom must be written in fields (model-recognizable English Danbooru identity tag, format character name (copyright name)), original characters do not write fandom. Actions, postures, scenes, temporary states (lying on carpet, standing, sitting, unzipped, wetness, injuries, etc.) must not be written into any fields - the file will be copied in every subsequent picture of him, and writing the posture in will make him maintain that posture in all pictures.\r\n   - Priority of file creation: current appearance specified in the target text > current character status in BaiBai Book > character card/World Info specified > reasonable completion. When the color is clearly written in the character design, it must be converted as it is and cannot be tampered with; hair and eyes are required, hair contains at least hair color and length/hair style, eyes must contain eye color, if any of the items is missing, the file will be discarded.\r\n   - If the setting does not include hair color, hairstyle or eye color, make up a concise, coordinated, long-term reusable color and hairstyle based on the world view, race, identity, personality and other character settings; this is a one-time file creation decision and cannot be re-randomized in the future.\r\n   - Use it directly after creating the file: in the same output, first establish the fixed appearance of the character in changes, and then in the picture ",
